<article class="env-definition" id="03UM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03UM">Definition <span data-tag="03UM">64.18.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Noetherian scheme. A <em>$\mathbf{Z}_\ell $-sheaf</em> on $X$, or simply an <em>$\ell $-adic sheaf</em> $\mathcal{F}$ is an inverse system $\left\{ \mathcal{F}_ n\right\} _{n\geq 1}$ where </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}_ n$ is a constructible $\mathbf{Z}/\ell ^ n\mathbf{Z}$-module on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the transition maps $\mathcal{F}_{n+1}\to \mathcal{F}_ n$ induce isomorphisms $\mathcal{F}_{n+1} \otimes _{\mathbf{Z}/\ell ^{n+1}\mathbf{Z}} \mathbf{Z}/\ell ^ n\mathbf{Z} \cong \mathcal{F}_ n$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> We say that $\mathcal{F}$ is <em>lisse</em> if each $\mathcal{F}_ n$ is locally constant. A <em>morphism</em> of such is merely a morphism of inverse systems. </p>
</article>